  "premise_review": [
    "Copy only the complete actual horizontal-preservation theorem. Preserve every exact implicit C/F/H/e and explicit E/nabla/X/s/h parameter, all original qualified types and the full original qualified proof call Folder.CrystallineTensor.heat_compatible_preserves_horizontal E nabla X s h.",
    "The conclusion is exactly nabla.horizontal X (e.map X s) and the premise h is exactly nabla.horizontal X s. This is genuine preservation of a supplied indexed predicate under the exact pointwise section map, obtained by an already supplied implication in E.",
    "Keep the entire original E : Folder.CrystallineTensor.HeatCompatibleEndomorphism H e type, including its independent commutation field and certificate. The wrapper already imports that provider; no narrower compatibility record, new legacy self-import, new199 provider or alias is substituted.",
    "The selected Connection provider supplies horizontal independently of Nabla, flat and integrable. No differential-kernel equation, analytic flatness, heat equation or crystalline geometry is inferred from the horizontal label. H remains a required original parameter even though no commutation equation is used to establish this conditional consequence.",
    "The other three wrappers are genuine proofs of independent identityAtZero, semigroupLaw and commutesWithHeat propositions. No zero/addition on Time, actual action composition formula or equality involving H.flow and e.map is encoded by those fields. All three complete statements/proofs stay exact archives.",
    "The organized Algebra.Groups label is historical lexical metadata, not evidence of a group/semigroup/action structure. Actual dependent predicate-preservation content belongs under dependent type theory and logical implication, with all original domain and supplied-proof limitations explicit.",
    "Only the containing namespace changes. Original import/documentation and exact source statement/proof bytes are retained; no provider substitution, missing premise, source-body edit, kernel replay or independent analytic theorem is introduced."
  ],
